{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassEndomorphism.HeckeBaerStarGeneric","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassEndomorphism.HeckeBaerStarGeneric","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Star.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.ZMod","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Matrix.Mul","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.ConjTranspose","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.ToLin","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Basis.VectorSpace","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Projection"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeBaerStarGeneric.not_hecke_baer_star_generic_sketch","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeBaerStarGeneric.not_hecke_baer_star_generic_sketch","kind":"theorem","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/hecke-baer-star-generic.lean#L233-L240","doc":"**The former axiom is false.** ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:hecke-baer-star-generic","label":"prop:hecke-baer-star-generic","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/hecke-baer-star-generic.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeBaerStarGeneric.not_baerStarRing_matrix_zmod_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeBaerStarGeneric.not_baerStarRing_matrix_zmod_two","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/hecke-baer-star-generic.lean#L213-L231","doc":"`M_2(𝔽₂)` with the transpose (trivial star on `𝔽₂`) is not Baer-*. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeBaerStarGeneric.symm_idem_annihilator_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeBaerStarGeneric.symm_idem_annihilator_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/hecke-baer-star-generic.lean#L206-L211","doc":"Over `𝔽₂`, a symmetric idempotent `2 × 2` matrix that kills\n`!![1,0;1,0]` on the right is zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeBaerStarGeneric.fact_prime_two_baer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeBaerStarGeneric.fact_prime_two_baer","kind":"instance","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/hecke-baer-star-generic.lean#L204-L204","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeBaerStarGeneric.failure_locus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeBaerStarGeneric.failure_locus","kind":"def","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/hecke-baer-star-generic.lean#L158-L176","doc":"The **exact** failure locus of Baer-* on the Iwahori--Hecke\nalgebra `H_n(q)`: `q` such that `q^{2k} = 1` for some\n`2 ≤ k ≤ n`.  Equivalently: primitive `2k`-th roots of unity\nfor `k ∈ [2, n]`.  At each such `q`, the symmetric quantum\ninteger `[k]_q = (q^k - q^{-k}) / (q - q^{-1})` vanishes,\nHoefsmit projectors fail, and the Jacobson radical becomes\nnon-trivial.\n\nBase ring (AGENTS.md §7c): the locus is cut out by the root-of-unity\nequations `q^{2k} = 1` alone, which need only a multiplicative\nmonoid — no inverses, no field.  It is therefore stated over\n`[Monoid R]`, the weakest class admitting the construction; the\nBaer-* statements below still instantiate it at their `[Field R]`.\n(The *reason* the locus matters — the vanishing of `[k]_q`, which\ndoes involve a quotient — lives in the surrounding theory, not in\nthis definition.)\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeBaerStarGeneric.bar_idempotent_transposition_partition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeBaerStarGeneric.bar_idempotent_transposition_partition","kind":"def","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/hecke-baer-star-generic.lean#L126-L154","doc":"**Bar-involution transpose property of the central idempotents**\n(`prop:explicit-central-idempotent` Step 1), named as a `Prop`.\n\nGiven a star-ring `A` (the bar involution `* : q ↦ q⁻¹` on `H_n(q)`),\na family of central primitive idempotents `e : List ℕ → A` indexed by\npartitions, and the partition-transpose map `transpose`, the property\nholds when the bar involution sends each idempotent to the one for the\ntransposed partition:\n\n  `star (e λ) = e (transpose λ)`.\n\nSelf-conjugate `λ = transpose λ` then gives a bar-fixed projection\n(`star (e λ) = e λ`); chiral pairs `(λ, transpose λ)` are bar-swapped.\n\nMathlib carries neither the Hecke central idempotents nor the bar\ninvolution on `H_n(q)`, so this **names** the proposition (per\nAGENTS.md §3b — \"naming is not a logical claim\") rather than asserting\na vacuous `True`.  A witness is the conjugate-pairing claim of\n`prop:explicit-central-idempotent`; instantiating `e`/`transpose` from\nthe Hoefsmit seminormal construction and discharging it is the open\nMathlib-formalisation step.\n\nRef: [leitner2026] §prop:explicit-central-idempotent \"Cross-checks\" §3-4;\n[murphy1981] Murphy elements and centre structure of symmetric-group /\nHecke algebras; [leitner2026] §rem:chirality-period-pairing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeBaerStarGeneric.matrix_algebra_baer_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeBaerStarGeneric.matrix_algebra_baer_right","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/hecke-baer-star-generic.lean#L59-L122","doc":"**Right annihilators in `M_n(K)` are idempotent-generated.** Was the axiom\n`matrix_algebra_baer_right_axiom`; proved 2026-11-15 (bean `qou-n2un`).\n\nLet `W ⊆ Kⁿ` be the span of the columns of the matrices in `S`, pick a\ncomplement `U`, and let `p` be the matrix of the projection onto `U`\nalong `W`. Then `x` kills every `s ∈ S` iff `x` kills `W` iff `x = x p`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeBaerStarGeneric.BaerStarRing.baer_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeBaerStarGeneric.BaerStarRing.baer_right","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/hecke-baer-star-generic.lean#L42-L42","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeBaerStarGeneric.BaerStarRing.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeBaerStarGeneric.BaerStarRing.mk","kind":"ctor","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/hecke-baer-star-generic.lean#L41-L41","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeBaerStarGeneric.BaerStarRing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeBaerStarGeneric.BaerStarRing","kind":"class","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/hecke-baer-star-generic.lean#L38-L46","doc":"A `*`-ring `A` is **Baer-*** when every right annihilator is\na principal right ideal generated by a *self-adjoint*\nidempotent. ","signatureChunk":0}]}